  "description_short": "Farm stall bakery between George and Mossel Bay serving fresh breads, pastries, and light meals.",
  "description_long": "Tucked away on the Klein Brak River road between George and Mossel Bay, De Kleine Loerie is a proper farm stall bakery where locals stop for fresh-baked goods and a decent cup of coffee. The smell of bread baking hits you as you walk in, and the display counters are stocked with everything from rusks and koeksisters to savoury pies and quiches.\n\nIt's the sort of place where you pop in for a loaf and end up leaving with a bag full of treats. The seating area is simple and relaxed, perfect for a quick breakfast or light lunch on your way through. They do a good line in preserves, local honey, and other farm stall staples if you're after provisions for the weekend.",
